# AI Pipeline

## Prompts
All prompts in `src/services/ai/prompts.ts` only. Never inline in hooks or components.

- System role is fixed and not user-overridable
- Transcript appended after instructions, delimited with `---`
- Every clinical prompt includes STRICT OUTPUT RULES (format only, no preamble/epilogue)
- Anti-hallucination: "Do not infer or add clinical findings not present in the transcript"
- Missing data → `[not documented]`, never invent vitals or diagnoses

## Output Validation
Every LLM response must pass `validateSOAPOutput()` in `src/services/ai/output-validator.ts` before display.

- Reject empty or < 50 char responses
- Require all SOAP sections: Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan
- Strip LLM meta-text ("Here is your note", disclaimers) before display
- On failure → return typed error, show retry UI (never show raw output)

## Memory Management
```typescript
let context = null;
try {
  context = await initWhisper({ filePath: modelPath });
  // ...
} finally {
  await context?.release();
}
```

- Never load Whisper and LLM simultaneously
- Pipeline: load → process → release → load next
- Model paths via `model-utils.ts` / device tier — never hardcoded in `whisper.ts` or `llm.ts`

## Audio
- ffmpeg output must be 16 kHz mono WAV before Whisper
- Chunking contract: `src/services/audio/chunker.ts`
- Check `src/utils/device-tier.ts` for lower-end device limits

## Eval
After changes to `whisper.ts`, `llm.ts`, or `prompts.ts`, suggest running eval against `eval/golden-dataset/`.

## Logging
Never log transcripts, SOAP output, or audio file paths in production builds.
